  "title": "",
  "body": "  For a mild illness that confers permanent immunity, the size of the recovered population can only grow. This question explores what happens when immunity is only temporary.   Will increase or decrease if    Suppose we shift 20000 susceptibles to the recovered population (so that and ), leaving unchanged. Now, will increase or will it decrease?   Using a total population of 50,000, give two other sets of values for , , and that lead to a decreasing .   In fact, the relative sizes of and determine whether will increase or decrease. Show that Explain your argument clearly. A suggestion: consider the rate equation for  .   "
