  "id": "ch7-predator-prey-ecology-3",
  "level": "2",
  "url": "ch7-sec-differential-equations-with-periodic-mboxsolutions.html#ch7-predator-prey-ecology-3",
  "type": "Exercise",
  "number": "7.3.6.25",
  "title": "",
  "body": "   The May model . The differential equations for this model are on page . Show that the constant functions are a solution to the equations. This is an equilibrium solution, as defined in the discussion of the pendulum (page ).   Is , an equilibrium solution?   Here is yet another equilibrium solution: Either verify that it is an equilibrium, or explain how it was derived.   "
