  "number": "10.5.6.14",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  In the text we used the alternating series for , , to approximate accurate to 7 decimal places. The claim was made that in taking the reciprocal to obtain an estimate for , the accuracy drops by one decimal place. In this problem you will see why this is true.   Consider first the more general situation where two functions are reciprocals, . Express in terms of and .   Use your answer in part a) to find an expression for the relative error in , , in terms of and . How does this compare to the relative error in ?   Apply your results in part b) to the functions and at . Since is about 7 times as large as , explain why the error in the estimate for should be about 7 times as large as the error in the estimate for  .   "
