  "title": "",
  "body": "  Our approach to integrating trigonometric polynomials was to express everything in the form . We can just as readily express everything in the form ( and integers—positive, negative, or 0), and develop our technique by dealing with various cases of this. See if you can work out the details, trying to parallel the approach developed in the text using sines and cosines as our basic functions.   "
