  "body": "  Let numberofsteps = 50 , and calculate the power spectrum one more time. What happens?  When we reduce the number of integration steps, new peaks appear in the power spectrum. These new peaks represent spurious information: the function has no components whose frequencies are 2\/3, 7\/3, or 8\/3. Let’s see why this happens. We’ll concentrate on . First, you must decide whether the peak in the power spectrum at comes from the sine or the cosine detector.   "
